course: dictionary
lesson: 1431
title: Carotene, the colour in carrots
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Carotene is an orange-yellow substance. It gives carrots, sweet potatoes and pumpkins their colour, and it is also found in many green leaves. Carotene is uncountable, so say «some carotene», not «a carotene».
explain: Use the clues in a sentence. «Carrots are orange because of beta-carotene.» Orange is the colour, and because tells you the carotene is the reason. So carotene is the substance that makes carrots orange.
explain: The second clue is about the body. «The body turns it into vitamin A, needed for the eyes.» Your body does not use carotene as it is. It changes it into vitamin A, which helps your eyes, skin and immune system.
explain: Be careful with myths. «Extra carrots do not give night vision.» Carrots help your eyes because of vitamin A, but eating more of them will not let you see in the dark.
fact: Carotene is an orange-yellow substance found in carrots, sweet potatoes, pumpkins and many green leaves.
fact: Carotene is a noun, and it is uncountable: say «some carotene», not «a carotene».
fact: The body turns carotene into vitamin A, which helps eyes, skin and the immune system.
fact: In autumn, the green chlorophyll in leaves fades, and the yellow and orange colours can show.
fact: Beta-carotene is one type of carotene: «Carrots are orange because of beta-carotene.»
exercise: What gives carrots their orange colour? | Vitamin A | Sugar | *Beta-carotene | Green chlorophyll
exercise: Which food contains carotene? | Glass of water | Sliced white bread | Plain boiled rice | *Pumpkin
exercise: What does the body turn carotene into? | Sugar | Iron | Chlorophyll | *Vitamin A
test: Jayden says, «Eat lots of carrots and you will see in the dark.» Is he right? | *No, extra carrots do not give night vision | Yes, if you eat them every day | Yes, but only if the carrots are cooked | Yes, carrots give perfect night vision
test: Which sentence uses carotene correctly? | Carotenes gives orange. | A carotene is in my lunchbox. | *Carrots contain some carotene. | Carotene are orange.
exam: Why do autumn leaves show yellow and orange when the green chlorophyll fades? | *Carotene is in the leaves, and its colour shows when the green fades | Wind paints the leaves in autumn | Carotene makes leaves green | Autumn leaves have no colour at all
